\subsection{Methods and Procedures}

\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item \textbf{Quantitative Testing:} Deploy prototypes; run scripts for load testing (e.g., 1,000 PPV requests). Collect and document all metrics via tools like Prometheus.
    
    \item \textbf{Qualitative Assessment:} User testing sessions (n=20); thematic analysis of feedback on pivots (e.g., RMRK ease of use).
    
    \item \textbf{Comparative Analysis:} Benchmark measured results against baselines (e.g., ERC-721 on Ethereum, centralised DRM systems).
    
    \item \textbf{Validity Measures:} Triangulation (multiple data sources); peer debriefing.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Analysis Approach}

All collected data will be analysed to:

\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=*]
    \item \textbf{Document achieved performance levels} across all KPI categories
    \item \textbf{Compare results} against existing solutions (Ethereum L2s, centralised DRM, bridge-based systems)
    \item \textbf{Identify trade-offs} between competing objectives (e.g., decentralisation vs. latency)
    \item \textbf{Assess feasibility} of the unified rights token approach for real-world deployment
    \item \textbf{Inform recommendations} for future development and adoption
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{Timeline and Resources}

\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item \textbf{Week 17:} Setup testnet; baseline tests and initial data collection.
    \item \textbf{Week 18:} User evaluations and qualitative data gathering.
    \item \textbf{Weeks 19--20:} Comprehensive data analysis; documentation of findings; refinements.
\end{itemize}

Resources: Free Kusama parachain via Canary Chaos program; open-source tools.

This plan ensures comprehensive validation through measurement and comparative analysis, informing the Discussion and Conclusion chapters with evidence-based findings.

